{"qid":"Q1514510","names":["County of Urgell"],"title":"County of Urgell","endonym":null,"capsule":"The County of Urgell was a Frankish march county in the eastern Pyrenees, centered on La Seu d'Urgell, created when Carolingian forces incorporated the Alt Urgell region between 785 and 790. Under the house of Ermengol, who ruled from 992, the county expanded southward at the expense of the taifa of Lleida and exercised suzerainty over Andorra, a protectorate it shared with the bishop of Urgell. The Ermengol line died out in 1231 with Countess Aurembiaix, who ceded the county to James I of Aragon, and two subsequent comital houses ruled under Aragonese overlordship. The last count, James II of Urgell, revolted against Ferdinand I of Aragon; his defeat in 1413 ended the county's separate existence, though the title continued nominally until 1809.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Boundaries are reasonably attested through Carolingian and Aragonese administrative records, though the precise eastern and southern extents fluctuated with Reconquista advances and are only broadly mapped.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: County of Urgell","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Urgell"},{"label":"Wikipedia: County of Urgell","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/County_of_Urgell"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"County of Urgell","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Guifré el Pilós (Wifred the Hairy)","nativeName":"","roman":"","start":870,"end":897,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Sunifred II","nativeName":"","roman":"","start":897,"end":948,"image":null